       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. SSUBCRWS.
       AUTHOR.     C HILLES.
       DATE-WRITTEN. SEPTEMBER, 1982.
       DATE-COMPILED.
      *INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
      *SECURITY.
      *REMARKS.
      *****************************************************************
      **          M O D I F I C A T I O N    H I S T O R Y
      *****************************************************************
      *    CHANGES:
      *      -IN SEPTEMBER, 1982, ADDED REQUESTING DEPT CAPABILITY.
      *       ADDED MORE LINES FOR CORP CODE AND QUANTITY.  AND
      *       GAVE A HIGH-USAGE AREA INDICATOR. CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    IN FEBRUARY, 1983, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *
      *       -  ON AN EXTRA PRINT ('X' IN 66TH BYTE OF PLANNER
      *          DATA), THE PGM NOW GOES TO THE KSAM FILE 'SPOOLFIL'
      *          TO DETERMINE WHERE TO PRINT THE EXTRA PRINTOUT.
      *
      *       -  NOW ALLOWS OVERRIDE FOR REQ & CHARGE DEPTS AND
      *          EXPENSE CLASS WHEN THERE IS A WORKORDER.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON NOV 28, 1983, CHANGED THE DEFAULT EXP CLASS LOGIC
      *    TO INCORPORATE SPECIAL KELLY LOGIC.  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON MARCH 26, 1984, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
      *
      *      1.  CONVERTED PGM TO "VIEW".
      *      2.  ADDED A CALL TO "TMTLSTAT" - MATERIAL STATUS INQUIRY.
      *          THE INQUIRY IS GOTTEN TO THRU AND f2.  NOTE THAT THIS
      *          ADDITION ALSO BRINGS IN RESERVATION INQUIRY, REQUIREMENTS
      *          ORDER INQUIRY, ETC FROM TMTLSTAT.
      *      3.  CHANGED THE PRINT FORMAT OF THE WORKSHEET.  THIS
      *          FORMAT CHANGE INCLUDES:
      *            -  SEPERATED EACH ITEM ON WORKSHEET BY A LINE OF
      *               ASTERICKS
      *            -  CODE, QUANTITY, LOCATION DATA GIVEN FIRST,
      *               ACCOUTING DATA ON LOWER LINE.
      *            -  EMPL AND SIGNATURE LINE TO ALLOW FOR THE
      *               PROCESS WORKSHEET OPTION TO NOT PRINT EACH ISSUE
      *               (AND USE THE WORKSHEET AS THE ONLY DOCUMENT).
      *     4.  CHANGED PGM TO BE COMPATIBLE WITH OTHER STORES PROGRAMS
      *         BY CALLING THE STORES EDITING SUBPROGRAMS "TIREDIT"
      *         (EDIT ACCOUNING DATA), AND "TQTYEDIT" (EDIT QUANTITY
      *         DATA)
      *     5.  THE PRINTOUT IS NOW SORTED BY PRIMARY LOCATION
      *         (TO AID STOREKEEPER IN FINDING ITEMS).
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON APR 24, 1984, CHANGED THE "DWLITEM-LIST" (DATA ITEM LIST
      *    FOR DWLITEM SEGMENT) TO "ALL-ITEMS" (PULL OUT ALL ITEMS
      *    IN DATA SET).  THIS IS BECAUSE THE TEST DATABASE HAD A
      *    DATA ITEM CHANGED IN DWLITEM, BUT IT WAS NOT CHANGED AT ALL
      *    PLANTS (YET).  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON APRIL 30, 1984, FIXED A PROBLEM -  WAS NOT PASSING THE
      *    WORKORDER TO "TQTYEDIT", THEREFORE COULD NOT WITHDRAW AN
      *    ITEM THAT WAS RESERVED FOR THAT WORKORDER.  THIS PROBLEM
      *    WAS FIXED BEFORE THIS PROGRAM WAS RELEASED TO ANY PLANT
      *    (EXCEPT AUSTRAILIA).  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON MAY 14, 1984, CHANGED PROGRAM TO PASS PLANNER DATA
      *    TO THE WORKSHEET PRINT SUBPROGRAM, SO THAT PLANNER DATA
      *    WILL BE PRINTED ON THE WORKSHEET.  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON MAY 24, 1984, CHANGED PROGRAM TO SKIP OVER WORKSHEET #
      *    0000 IMMEDIATELY AFTER THE 9999 WORKSHEET.  IN THE PAST,
      *    THIS WOULD RESULT IN A BLOWUP MESSAGE, ALTHOUGH THE
      *    NEXT TRY TO CREATE A WORKSHEET WOULD WORK, BECAUSE THE
      *    SW# WAS INCREMENTED BEFORE THE BLOWUP.  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON OCT 10, 1984, CHANGED THIS PROGRAM AS PART OF THE
      *    COMBINATION OF AKRON AND PLANT VERSIONS OF STORES
      *    PROGRAMS.  THE CHANGES ARE AS FOLLOWS:
      *
      *        1.  THE "DEFAULT EXPENSE CLASS" LOGIC WAS MOVED FROM
      *            THIS SUBPROGRAM INTO THE "TIREDIT" EDITING SUB-
      *            PROGRAM.  THIS REQUIRED ADDING THE "STR-EXP-CLASS"
      *            AS A PARAMETER TO THE CALL OF "TIREDIT".
      *            (DEFAULT EXP CLASS IS NOT USED IN AKRON, AND THE
      *            EDITING SUB-PROGRAM WILL HANDLE THESE DIFFERENCES).
      *
      *        2.  THE "TIREDIT", "TQTYEDIT", "TWSPRT" SUBPROGRAMS WERE
      *            CHANGED WITH SPECIAL LOGIC FOR AKRON.
      *
      *        3.  IN THE PRINT ROUTINE, IF AKRON A "CENTER" HEADING
      *            IS ADDED FOR THE WORK CENTER FIELD.
      *
      *        4.  A DIFFERENT FORMS FILE IS MAINTAINED FOR AKRON AND THE
      *            PLANTS.  THE AKRON VERSION HAS A "WORK CENTER" FIELD.
      *            THE PLANT VERSION HAS THIS FIELD, BUT IT IS DISPLAY
      *            ONLY, NO ENHANCEMENTS (INVISIBLE).  (THUS THE SCREEN
      *            BUFFER IS THE SAME IN THE PROGRAM).  THE AKRON VERSION
      *            HAS A 1 BYTE "CHARGE TYPE FIELD".  THE PLANTS VERSION
      *            HAS A 2 BYTE EXTENSION TO THE CHARGE DEPT.  SO ON
      *            THE AKRON FORM FILE, THE SECOND HALF THE THIS EXTENSION
      *            FIELD WAS CHANGED TO  DISPLAY ONLY, NO ENHANCEMENTS.
      *            (ONCE AGAIN, SO THAT THE SCREEN BUFFER DOES NOT NEED
      *            TO BE DIFFERENT FOR THE TWO VERSIONS).
      *
      *        5.  THE AKRON FORMS FILE ALSO CONTAINS A "STOREROOM"
      *            FIELD - SINCE PERSONNEL IN AKRON CAN PRINT WORKSHEETS
      *            AT MULTIPLE STOREROOMS (EVEN MULTIPLES PER DATABASE).
      *            THIS FIELD IS INVISIBLE ON THE PLANT VERSION.  IF
      *            AKRON, THIS FIELD IS USED TO DETERMINE WHERE TO PRINT
      *            THE WORKSHEET.
      *            CIH.
      *
      *    ADDED THE PLANT 5 STOREROOM PRINTER TO THE PRINT LOCATIONS
      *    FOR AKRON.  THIS WILL BE ACCESSED BY PUTTING IN "50" AS THE
      *    PRINT-LOC.  NOTE - NEED TO DEVELOP A FLEXIBLE METHOD OF
      *    DIRECTING WORKSHEET PRINTOUTS FOR MULTIPLE PLANT SITUATIONS,
      *    AND GET THIS OUT OF BEING HARD-CODED|  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON DECEMBER 10, 1984,
      *    CHANGED THIS PROGRAM TO USE THE LOCAL PRINTER (SCREEN PRINT
      *    PRINTER) TO PRINT THE WORKSHEET IF THE HOME GROUP IS "DBT".
      *    THIS IS THE TRAINING DATABASE, AND FOR TRAINING WE WOULD LIKE
      *    THE WORKSHEETS TO PRINT AT THE LOCAL PRINTER, AND NOT IN THE
      *    ACTUAL STOREROOM.  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON JANUARY 21, 1985, ADDED A DUMMY PARAMETER TO THE CALL
      *    OF THE SUBPROGRAM "TMTLSTAT" - MATERIAL STATUS INQUIRY.
      *    THIS IS A DUMMY CORPORATE CODE PARAMETER - USED BY PROGRAMS
      *    THAT MAY PASS THE CORP CODE TO THE INQUIRY, THUS BYPASSING
      *    THE CORPORATE CODE ENTRY SCREEN.  IF THE PASSED CODE IS SPACES,
      *    THE CODE ENTRY SCREEN IS BROUGHT, AND THE CODE PARAMETER IS
      *    IGNORED.  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON JANUARY 23, 1985, CHANGED THE "K-TERMINAL" PARAMETER
      *    FOR THE CALL TO "TSPLPRT" TO 9(4) FROM 9(2).  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON MARCH 16, 1985, CHANGED THIS PROGRAM TO CALL "TSHWRDFM"
      *    TO DO THE SHOWFORM, READFIELDS, AND VARIOUS FUNCTION KEY
      *    PROCEDURES (IE. FLIP SCREEN).  THIS IS BECAUSE THE PROGRAM
      *    WAS BLOWING UP OFTEN ON VIEW ERROR 153 AND 154 ON THE
      *    "VREADFIELDS".  THE SUBPROGRAM "TSHWRDFM" MAKES 5 ATTEMPTS
      *    AT THE "VREADFIELDS" BEFORE BLOWING DOWN.  THERE ARE ALSO
      *    VIEW ERRORS MANY TIMES ON THE OPEN TERMINAL CALL, AND
      *    FEWER TIMES ON THE "VSHOWFORM" CALL.  IF THIS CHANGE PROVES
      *    SUCCESSFUL, I WILL PROBABLY THEN ADD LOGIC TO HANDLE
      *    THESE PROBLEMS ALSO.  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    ON AUGUST 16, 1985, CHANGED THE HIGH-USAGE CHECK IN THE
      *    PROGRAM.  THE PROGRAM NOW CHECKS STR-HIGH-USAGE TO
      *    DETERMINE IF THE ITEM IS A HIGH-USAGE ITEM.  DALE HOERLE.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *   10/ 8/85  ADDED CALLS TO FINDJCW, NLAPPEND, CATOPEN, AND
      *             CATCLOSE IN ORDER TO ACCOMODATE THE NATIVE
      *             LANGUAGE SUPPORT FACILITY.  ADDED LINKAGES AND
      *             ALSO MADE THE CHANGE TO THE FORMFILE NAMES.
      *             CHANGED ALL REFERENCES OF TSCRPRNT TO TSCRPRT2,
      *             TDATECHK TO TDATECK2, TSHWRDFM TO TSHWRDF2.
      *             THIS WAS TO INCORPORATE THE NATIVE LANGUAGE
      *             SUPPORT VERSIONS OF THESE SUBROUTINES.
      *                                             PD RAGLOW.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    1/2/86.
      *       CHANGED THIS PROGRAM TO A SUBPROGRAM, SO THAT MMIS
      *       PROGRAMS CAN CALL IT, PASSING WORKORDER NUMBER AND PART
      *       NUMBERS THAT THE USERS ALREADY HAS ON SCREEN, AND THAT
      *       DATA WILL BE INITIALLY DISPLAYED ON THE SCREEN.  THE NAME
      *       OF THIS PROGRAM IS CHANGED FROM "TISSCRWS" TO "TSUBCRWS",
      *       AND A NEW MAIN PROGRAM HAS BEEN CREATED TO CALL THIS
      *       SUBPROGRAM.  THE MAIN PROGRAM WILL RETAIN THE NAME
      *       "TISSCRWS".  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    07/23/86.
      *      ADDED MULTIPLE STOREROOM CAPABILITY TO THE PROGRAM.  A
      *      MULTIPLE-STOREROOM PLANT IS DETERMINED BY THE EXISTANCE OF THE
      *      KEY "STST" IN THE "MPLTINFO" DATASET.  IF SO, THE USER MAY ENTER
      *      A MNEMONIC FOR THE STOREROOM HE WISHES TO PRINT AT.  DIFFERENT
      *      PREFIXES TO BIN LOCATIONS ARE USED TO STORE THE QUANTITIES AT THE
      *      DIFFERENT STOREROOMS.  THE WORKSHEET WILL ONLY ALLOW QUANTITES
      *      TO BE WITHDRAWN FROM THE STOREROOM THE USER IS PRINTING AT .
      *      THIS IS HANDLED BY "TQTYEDIT" SUBPROG.  CIH.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *    08/18/86.
      *      ADDED THE STORES CODE INQUIRY SUSBSYSTEM AS THE "f3" FUNCTION
      *      FROM THIS PROGRAM.                     D.A. PLUM.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C  08/18/92  BK DISMUKES   REQUEST #
      *C     1. CHANGED 64-CODE-LOOP JUST BEFORE "CALL TIREDIT"
      *C        MODIFIED "MOVE DE-CODE (1)" TO READ "MOVE DE-CODE (SUB1)"
      *C        SO THAT ALL CODES ARE CHECKED.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C  08/25/92  BK DISMUKES   REQUEST #6252
      *C     1. ADDED LOGIC TO PASS STR-RESTRICTED-FLG TO TIREDIT.
      *C        STR-RESTRICTED-FLG DEFINES STORES ITEMS THAT HAVE
      *C        RESTRICTIONS ON WHO CAN WITHDRAW THEM.  THIS IS PART
      *C        OF THE RESTRICTED WITHDRAWAL STOREROOM SYSTEM
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C  03/05/93  BK DISMUKES   REQUEST #6380
      *C     1. CORRECTED LOGIC TO DISPLAY EXP-CLASS AFTER TIREDIT
      *C        CALL.
      *C     2. DEFAULT CHARGE-TYPE TO "3" FOR AKRON PLANTS WHEN
      *C        USER IS SIGNED ONTO A WORKORDER.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   04NOV1994    WILL MCINTYRE   REQUEST 94-027
      *C     ADDED CODE TO PASS NEW PARMS TO TQTYEDIT, TO CHECK FOR LIMITS
      *C     ON STOREROOM RETURNS.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   06/12/96     JEFF BUNGO
      *C     EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C     INCLUDE CENTURY ON WORKSHEET DATE.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   03/20/97     JEFF BUNGO
      *C     FOR MULTI DB PLANTS (AKRON), DO OVRDBF TO PROPER PLANT LIB
      *C     TO CREATE WORKSHEET FOR THE PLANT STOREROOM SPECIFIED ON
      *C     FIELD DE-STOREROOM.  THE VALUE IN DE-STOREROOM (XX) IS
      *C     FOUND IN MPLTINFO WITH KEY STXX TO FIND WHERE TO PRINT
      *C     AND WHICH LIBRARY THE PLANT'S DATABASE IS IN.  FOR EXAMPLE
      *C     IN AKRON DE-STOREROOM 10 IS FOR PLANT 1 STOREROOM.
      *C     MPLTINFO KEY ST10 WOULD BE RETRIEVED TO GET THE PRINTER
      *C     NUMBER AND THE LIBRARY WHERE PLANT 1 EXISTS (MCPRD1).
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   04/14/97     JEFF BUNGO
      *C     OVRDBF FOR ADDITIONAL FILES FOUND IN CDESC WHEN PRINTING
      *C     THE WORKSHEET.  IF A PLANT WAS CREATING A WORKSHEET FOR
      *C     ANOTHER DATABASE, THE CODE DESCRIPTION WOULD BE BLANK
      *C     IF THE CODE DID NOT EXIST IN THE ORIGINATING DATABASE.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C  05/02/97      JEFF BUNGO
      *C     RETRIVE FRANCHISE TABLE AND PASS NEW PARAMETERS TO
      *C     TQTYEDIT FOR CHECK OF FRANCHISE BINS.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   OCTOBER 1995  JIM COFFMAN
      *C     CHANGED ISSPARTS PARAMETERS TO BE INCLUDED IN A COPYLIB
      *C     MEMBER. THIS WAS NECESSARY TO ALLOW THE AREA TO BE
      *C     EXPANDABLE TO CONTAIN THE LINK TO A WORK ORDER LOGIC
      *C     REQUEST NOW AVAILABLE IN AN E1 REQUISITION CREATE.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   JANUARY 28, 1997  JEFF BUNGO (REQUEST)
      *C     ADDED EXPENSE CLASS ENTRY FIELDS FOR EACH CODE ON THE
      *C     WORKSHEET.  IF THESE FIELDS ARE LEFT BLANK, THEN USE
      *C     THE MAIN EXPENSE CLASS ENTERED.  IF NOT BLANK, THEN
      *C     EDIT EACH EXP CLASS.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   03/11/1998   CA YODER   REQ #97-1125
      *C     CHANGED PASSWORD FROM 6 TO 8 FOR CALL TO "TPERPASS."
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   04/23/1999   CA YODER
      *C     FOR SAP R/3 PLANTS, WRITE STOREROOM WITHDRAWAL RECORDS
      *C     TO MEMBER IN FILE SWDATAFL.  ALSO, IF SPECIFIED IN
      *C     MPLTINFO, DO NOT PRINT WORKSHEET.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   02JUL02  DAVE PLUM
      *C   REVISED PARAGRAPH 9999-PUT-SWPFM-REC TO NO LONGER MOVE SPACES
      *C   TO THE CHARGE DEPT WHEN THE EXPENSE CLASS IS AN SAP CWIP
      *C   (INTERNAL ORDER) NUMBER.  SAP STILL WANTS A VALID DEPARTMENT
      *C   TO BE PASSED.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   07/10/2002   CA YODER
      *C     FOR SAP R/3 PLANTS, BLANK OUT BIN NUMBER ON BUF-DWLITEM
      *C     IF THERE IS NO QUANTITY FOR THE BIN.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   03/05/2003   CA YODER
      *C     FOR SAP R/3 PLANTS, USE DWLITEM EMPLOYEE NUMBER TO LOOK
      *C     UP EMPLOYEE NAME.  TYLER FOUND EXAMPLES OF INCORRECT
      *C     NAMES BEING SENT OVER TO SAP.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *C   04/26/2005   CA YODER   REQ #2005-72391
      *C     FOR SAP R/3 PLANTS, CHANGE WORDING ON SCREEN FROM "EXP
      *C     CLASS" TO "SAP INT ORD # (CWIP/EWIP)".
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
DCR01 *  AUG 10, 2005    DCR01     DAN RAUCH   REQ#: 2005-18721799-0001
DCR01 *  USE CLOCK NUMBER ENTERED TO RETRIEVE WORK ORDER DATA
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
CAY02 *  JAN 11, 2006    CAY02     CA YODER    REQ#: 2005-16814824-0065
CAY02 *  DISABLE AKRON-SPECIFIC LOGIC IN PREPARATION FOR SAP CONVERSION.
CAY02 *  IF IT'S AN AKRON PLANT, MOVE "999" TO THE SRF PLANT CODE SO
CAY02 *  THAT THE AKRON LOGIC DOES NOT EXECUTE.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
CAY03 *  01/04/2010      CAY03    CA YODER     REQ#: 2010-00142425-001
CAY03 *     UPDATE LOGIC ASSIGNING WORKORDER LETTER SUFFIX.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
CAY109*  10/09/2012      CAY109   CA YODER     REQ#: 2010-00142425-001
CAY109*     ADD AN INDICATOR FOR EXPENSE TYPE:  PM OR BREAKDOWN.
CAY109*     INCLUDE INDICATOR IN INTERFACE FILE TO SAP.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
CAY707*  07/07/2014      CAY707   CA YODER     REQ#: 2014-04989692-001
CAY707*                                        RFC#: 1102576; CD#: 5100187
CAY707*     ADD "OTHER" AS A VALUE FOR EXPENSE TYPE.  OPERATOR MUST
CAY707*     TYPE PM, BD, OR OT; SPACES NOT AN ALLOWED VALUE.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
DB1008*    10/08/2021   DB1008    D BARAONA    REQ#: 2020-01196736
DB1008*                                        RFC#: 1122593; CD#: 5106272
DB1008*      BEFORE ALLOWING A STOREROOM WIITHDRAWAL, CHECK IF THE
DB1008*      USER'S PERSONNEL RECORD (MCFPMM0300) IS FLAGGED AS RESTRICTED
DB1008*      IN THE PERPAD FIELD. IF Y, THEY ARE NOT ALLOWED TO WITHDRAW.
      *----------------------------------------------------------------
      *  MMM DD, CCYY    XXX01     XXXNAMEXXXX   REQUEST# 200?-99999
      *      XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXDESCXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
      *****************************************************************
       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
       COPY SPECIALN IN COPYLIB.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT MPLTINFO-PK-I
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MSTORERM-CD-I
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MWRKLIST-WK-O
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0301
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DWLITEM-WK-O
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1501
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                 WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT PER-PERSON-PC-I
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLMM0301
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

DCR01      SELECT CURRENT-LABOR  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLMM1601
DCR01             ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
DCR01             ACCESS MODE  IS DYNAMIC
DCR01             RECORD KEY   IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
DCR01                          WITH DUPLICATES
DCR01             FILE STATUS  IS FILE-STATUS.

DCR01      SELECT BASIC-WO       ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLMM1001
DCR01             ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
DCR01             ACCESS MODE  IS DYNAMIC
DCR01             RECORD KEY   IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
DCR01                          WITH DUPLICATES
DCR01             FILE STATUS  IS FILE-STATUS.

DCR01      SELECT PLANNED-WO     ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLMM1101
DCR01             ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
DCR01             ACCESS MODE  IS DYNAMIC
DCR01             RECORD KEY   IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
DCR01                          WITH DUPLICATES
DCR01             FILE STATUS  IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DISPLAY-FILE
               ASSIGN TO WORKSTATION-ZISSCRWS-SI
               ORGANIZATION IS TRANSACTION
               ACCESS IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS DISPLAY-STATUS
               CONTROL-AREA IS WS-CONTROL.

           SELECT SWPFM-O
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-SWDATAFL
               ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL
               ACCESS MODE IS SEQUENTIAL
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
      *------ FD AREA FOR IBM ONLY ------*
       FD  DISPLAY-FILE
           LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED.
       01  DISPLAY-REC                   PIC X(1000).

       FD  MPLTINFO-PK-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MPLTINFO-PK-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0500  OF MCFLCS0501.

       FD  MSTORERM-CD-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MSTORERM-CD-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0200  OF MCFLCS0201.

       FD  MWRKLIST-WK-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MWRKLIST-WK-REC-O.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS0300  OF MCFLCS0301.

       FD  DWLITEM-WK-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DWLITEM-WK-REC-O.
           COPY DDS-MCRPCS1500  OF MCFLCS1501.

       FD  PER-PERSON-PC-I
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  PER-PERSON-PC-REC-I.
           COPY DDS-MCRPMM0300  OF MCFLMM0301.


DCR01  FD  CURRENT-LABOR
DCR01      LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
DCR01  01  CURRENT-LABOR-REC.
DCR01      COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLMM1601.


DCR01  FD  BASIC-WO
DCR01      LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
DCR01  01  BASIC-WO-REC.
DCR01      COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLMM1001.


DCR01  FD  PLANNED-WO
DCR01      LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
DCR01  01  PLANNED-WO-REC.
DCR01      COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLMM1101.

       FD  SWPFM-O.
       01  SWPFM-REC-O          PIC X(187).

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

       77  HANDLE-BLOWUP-FLAG            PIC X(1)  VALUE "Y".
       77  MMIS-PASSWORD                 PIC X(8)  VALUE "DO-ALL; ".
       77  DISP-SC                       PIC -9999 VALUE ZEROS.
       77  ISS-QTY-SAVE                  PIC 9(8)  VALUE ZEROS.
       77  RSRVD-THIS-WO                 PIC S9(8) VALUE ZERO.
       77  AVAIL                         PIC S9(8) VALUE ZERO.
       77  AVAIL-THIS-WO                 PIC S9(8) VALUE ZERO.
       77  SUB                           PIC 99    VALUE ZEROS.
       77  SUB1                          PIC 99    VALUE ZEROS.
       77  SUB2                          PIC 99    VALUE ZEROS.
       77  SUB4                          PIC 99    VALUE ZEROS.
       77  SUB5                          PIC 99    VALUE ZEROS.
       77  DUP-SUB                       PIC 99    VALUE ZEROS.
       77  FRAN-SUB                      PIC 9     VALUE ZEROS.
       77  TABLE-LIMIT                   PIC S9(4) VALUE ZEROS.
       77  ONHAND-ERR1-FLAG              PIC X(1)  VALUE "N".
       77  ONHAND-ERR2-FLAG              PIC X(1)  VALUE "N".
       77  PRINTER-FOUND-FLAG            PIC X(1)  VALUE "N".
       77  MOVED-IT-FLAG                 PIC X(1).
       77  PRINTER-IN-FILE               PIC X(2)  VALUE SPACES.
       77  TOTAL-QTY                     PIC 9(8)  VALUE 0.
       77  SPOOL-PRT-STORERM             PIC S9(2) VALUE 0 BINARY.
       77  SPOOL-PRT-LOCAL               PIC S9(2) VALUE 0 BINARY.
       77  HOLD-QTY                      PIC X(8).
       77  SAVE-VIEW-LASTKEY             PIC S9(4) BINARY VALUE 0.
       77  SAVE-FORM                     PIC X(16) VALUE SPACES.
       77  SAVE-REQ-SYNR3-SW             PIC X(1).
CAY02  77  DUMMY-PLT-NUM                 PIC X(3)  VALUE "999".
CAY03 *---- 01/04/2010:  ADDED PARAMETER FOR CMMISYR.
CAY03  77  MMIS-LETTER                PIC X.

       COPY FUNCTDEF IN COPYLIB.
      **************************************************************
      **                                                          **
      **         M I S C E L L A N E O U S                        **
      **                                                          **
      **************************************************************

       01  PARA-POS-1.
           05  FILLER                    PIC X(9)  VALUE "ERROR IN ".
           05  SAVE-PARA-1               PIC X(51) VALUE SPACES.

      *------ PARMS FOR CALL TO 'QCMDEXC': EXECUTE A COMMAND
       01  COMMAND-WORK                  PIC X(70).
       01  COMMAND-LEN      PIC S9(10)V9(5) COMP-3 VALUE 70.


       01  PARA-POS-2.
           05  SAVE-PARA-2               PIC X(60) VALUE SPACES.

      **************************************************************
      **                                                          **
      **            D A T E / T I M E   A R E A S                 **
      **                                                          **
      **************************************************************

       01  YMD-DATE.
           05  YMD-SHORT.
               10  YY-SHORT.
                   15  FILLER            PIC X(1).
